{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-13T16:16:31.368Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**`src/core/foundation/doctor-languages.ts`** (new) — exports `checkLanguages(projectRoot, config)`, returning `DoctorCheckResult[]` (zero or one, the same shape `checkValidatorRuns` produces). It reads `readLanguageMap` and `uncoveredBy` from task 1's `src/kernel/languages/` (unchanged), adds a check only when a language other than TypeScript/JavaScript is present, and builds the message per the cli-foundation requirement: languages joined by `, `, then `. <language> lacks gates: ...; extras: ...` per other language, omitting the empty part. It passes with a warning when some language lacks a gate, so it never changes doctor's exit code. Tagged with both scenarios and ADRs 006 and 017.\n\n**`src/core/foundation/doctor-changes.ts`** (new) — `checkLocks`, `checkArchives`, `checkDoneMarkers` moved byte-for-byte from `doctor.ts` (with their shared `make`/`exists` helpers), exported.\n\n**`src/core/foundation/doctor.ts`** — dropped from 250 to 178 lines: removed the moved functions, the now-unused imports (`fs`, `isPidRunning`, `parseFrontmatter`, `listChanges`), and the local `make`/`exists`; imports the three checks and helpers back from `doctor-changes.ts`; `runDoctorChecks` spreads `checkLanguages` in one line right after the `checkGit` line.\n\n**`tests/doctor-languages.test.ts`** (new) — three plain `node:test` cases through `runDoctorChecks` with injected `loadConfig`/`probeValidator`: \"Rust beside TypeScript\" (asserts the exact warning message and that `report.ok` equals its value without the check), and both \"Pure TypeScript project\" cases (only `package.json`; no manifest) asserting no `languages` check. Temp projects run their own `git init`/commit with the redirecting `GIT_*` variables stripped.\n\nBoth verifies pass: the task's `tests/doctor-languages.test.ts` (3 pass) and the proposal's `pnpm verify` (exit 0, full suite, lint, typecheck, build). Result file written to `.run/results/2.md`."}}
